I just did two test installs of RH7.2 (from boxed CDs) on my
UP2000 using SRM, and I had no such problems.  I don't know
anything about an APB loader, as I have always used the SRM and
aboot combination.

Could the CDs you burned be bad?  Could they be missing a
bootblock?  On this newsgroup and/or the axp-list@redhat.com
mailing list, there has been mention of a special method to make
an ISO image bootable.  I don't know whether that needs to be done
on downloaded ISOs burned to CDs.

If you can get to an SRM prompt, put a known good CD in the
drive.  At a price of $30-40, I think buying known good CDs is a
good deal.  Then, type "boot dka400 -fl i" (modify the device name
to fit your system).  At the aboot prompt, type "l" to get a list
of options.  Usually, option 0 is the best one.

Good luck.

Robert Riches
rm.riches@verizon.net


