Which CD? That means from what distro?  I assume that you are talking
about current RH 7.2.  It should boot with

   boot dka500 -fl 0

command.  Try 'b dka500 -fl i' if you need to pick up some other
variants from a list (an installation in a "text" mode, for example).

> it gets to the point where it asks:
> 
> "What Type of Media Contains the Packages to be Installed".

It should not really ask for that either.  Either something is
wrong or you have some _really old_ CD.

> It then asks for a driver,

If you are seeing that without picking up an "expert mode" of an
installation then either you are hacking with something long
obsolete or you have some unspecified firmware/hardware problems.

> I've checked by looking at "show config" and the cdrom (RRD43) is 
> definately connected to the NCR53C810 SCSI controller.

This one needs 'ncr53c8xx' module and NOT 'sym53c8xx'.  There is
a long list of "middle range" controllers covered by both these
drivers but some low end, like 810, and some hig end require
a specific one.  Unfortunately version 2 'sym53c8xx' driver,
a.k.a. 'sym53c8xx_2', is not available on any "public" installation
media.

> * At this point there is an additional field that says,
> 
> "Specific Module Parameters"
> "Miscellanous_____________________"

There are no extra parameters you could use here.  This is a PCI
controller.

   Michal


