This problem can occur on Intel boxes, but doesn't tend to crop up
because when you compile ECN support on Intel it's off by default,
whereas for some bizarre reason it's on by default when you compile for
the Alpha.  Next time you build a new kernel, set it to off by default.

I came across this when I installed a new wireless firewall/router at
home, and found that my Linux/i386 machine and Windows machine would
talk to it, but my Linux/Alpha machine would not.

Tim



