I think you need a little bit more explanations.

1st Open VMS what do you have as operating system on your AXP is
an old but really great OS. If you like to have more informations
about it and the error messages you should ask in
news:comp.os.vms.

2nd If you dont and you like to move to linux you�re welcome
here.

Redhat is an Operating System like Unix or VMS (some people even
count Windows with it). The current release for AXP is 7.2. You
have to watch that you have the right version for your hardware.
Linux is available for some different hardware platforms - Intel
and Alpha are just two of them.

If you like install Redhat Linux on your AXP (and to replace VMS
with it) you have to boot the Redhat install CD from the SRM
console. You can access this SRM console by pressing the HALT
button or in the beginning of the boot process by pressing CTL+P
(I hope I remember right - someone correct me!).

If you are on SRM you see a prompt like >>>. There you can see,
what devices are connected. Just type >>> sh dev dk. You should
see some DKA and DKB devices. Probably DKA400 or 500 or DKB400 or
500 is your CDROM. If have indentified it just type >>boot dka400
(or what you have found) and follow the installation process.

Good luck and have fun!


Bye

