What level of performance degradation have you observed by using
the -mieee switch?

My main encounter with it was in connection with the Rainbow
document indexing package, which uses a lot of floating point in
its document similarity computation.  I saw just a few cases that
would blow up without -mieee, so I added it to the Makefile and
recompiled the whole package (something akin to "make clean ;
make", IIRC).  I saw only about a 2% performance degradation on
those parts that had worked without the switch.  Based on that
number, I formed the opinion that the degradation was not very
serious.

