> My main encounter with it was in connection with the Rainbow
> document indexing package, which uses a lot of floating point in its
> document similarity computation.  I saw just a few cases that would
> blow up without -mieee, so I added it to the Makefile and recompiled
> the whole package (something akin to "make clean ; make", IIRC).  I
> saw only about a 2% performance degradation on those parts that had
> worked without the switch.  Based on that number, I formed the
> opinion that the degradation was not very serious.

Perhaps you were using an EV6. The EV6 has precise trap reporting, so
the trap barriers are nops, which can be ignored very efficiently. The
effect is much larger on EV5, where it kills the pipelining.

