> > > Don't use the onboard IDE for disks.  Writing to a disk there will
> > give errors.  This is caused by a chipset bug.  Any disk controllers
> > should go in the 32-bit PCI slots, where the PCI-PCI bridge will stop
> > the errors.
> > 
>     	
> is'nt it possible to put aboot in the rom?

I suppose you could put it there, but you couldn't use it.  Aboot
depends on SRM to load the kernel image into ram.  It uses SRM
functions to access disks, so the kernel has to be on a disk
usable by SRM.  You could prepare a hard disk with just aboot and a
kernel and boot off that with the root partition on a different disk.
The kernel is small, so it's not hard to get it onto the disk without
errors, or you can turn off DMA for that disk.  It's only DMA
transfers crossing a page boundary that break, so using PIO mode is
safe.  Reading from a device is also safe.

-- 
