In response to a bug report I had filed or commented on, somebody
at Redhat (possibly Mike Harris, but I'm not certain) stated that
_all_ Redhat packages are compiled with -mieee just to avoid
exceptions that shouldn't be fatal.  I think the issue I had
filed was that taking the log() of a large negative number (less
than roughly 610, IIRC) would otherwise produce a denormallized
number, and taking the exp() of that would bomb.

Anyway, using -mieee would seem to put one in pretty good
company.

