> I also encounter strange seg faults on freeing memory. Which works
> fine on my intel box, but cores on my alpha (Miata 500MHz).

Is this when you write your own programs?  Because of the larger
address space on Alphas (43 bits for ev56) things often get laid out
differently from on a 32-bit system.  I've seen many cases where an
error goes by undetected on intel systems but produces a segfault on
Alpha.  The problem is usually a buffer overrun somewhere, or using
free()'d memory.  Check your code with electric fence.

